keel-keys (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The package is now built from Keel-Linux/keel-keys, not from
    keel-transition (handbook decision 0055). The binary package keeps
    its name, keel-archive-keyring, and the version continues above
    0.2.0.
  * One keyring file for each signing role: keel-archive-keyring.gpg
    (main, the same file as before), keel-images-keyring.gpg,
    keel-security-keyring.gpg and keel-testing-keyring.gpg. The keys are
    not merged into one keyring.
  * /usr/share/keel-archive-keyring/fingerprint keeps the main primary
    key fingerprint only. The new FINGERPRINTS file beside it has 1 line
    for each role.
  * The build fails when a key file holds more or less than 1 primary
    key, holds secret key material, or has a fingerprint that is not the
    fingerprint in FINGERPRINTS and in debian/rules.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
